Breathing exercises. Different languages have different breathing patterns. Because

2
00:00:04,280 --> 00:00:07,720
Americans are a little louder than you may expect, in order to emulate this

3
00:00:07,720 --> 00:00:11,020
projection of the voice, you're going to have to take deeper breaths than you're

4
00:00:11,020 --> 00:00:15,980
accustomed to. Stand up straight, chest out, inhale deeply, and in a deep voice

5
00:00:15,980 --> 00:00:20,680
say, hi, how's it going? As you saw with phrasing, your breathing should be in sync

6
00:00:20,680 --> 00:00:24,520
with the phrasing and punctuation. If you're saying something short, you can get

7
00:00:24,520 --> 00:00:28,480
away with a more shallow inhale, but short panting breaths are interpreted as nervous

8
00:00:28,480 --> 00:00:32,820
or impatient, whereas long, deep exhalations of sound are considered calm

9
00:00:32,820 --> 00:00:37,280
and confident. Take deeper breaths than usual and push the sound out from deep in

10
00:00:37,280 --> 00:00:41,200
your chest. Pay particular attention that you do not push the air out through your

11
00:00:41,200 --> 00:00:44,560
